From a5e69bfe9076e646b9855445cc555e9cab526c39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:48:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] perf(gateway): keep idle connections to instances and the
 control plane

The stream proxy and the control-plane clients kept at most two idle
connections per host (the net/http default), so after a burst of
concurrent requests most connections were closed and the next burst
had to dial again. Both now keep up to 64 idle connections per host.
The control-plane reverse proxy and the resolver use their own
transport based on http.DefaultTransport, and the reverse proxy stops
waiting for response headers after 30s.
